### SC4: Code Typing Animation — Interaction

**Gap Coverage:** N/A (Greenfield)

**Target State:**
```
app/components/diamond/
└── ScreenSafeTyping.tsx       # aria-hidden + sr-only pattern
app/globals.css
└── .typing-animation           # CSS keyframes
```

**DoD (Sequenced):**
- [ ] Pass 1: CSS animation skeleton
  - [ ] `@keyframes typing` with `steps(40)`
  - [ ] `.typing-animation` class with `width: 0 → 100%`
  - [ ] `overflow: hidden`, `white-space: nowrap`

- [ ] Pass 2: Screen-safe implementation
  - [ ] `ScreenSafeTyping.tsx` with `aria-hidden="true"` wrapper
  - [ ] Parallel `sr-only` `pre > code` with complete code
  - [ ] Reduced motion: `animation: none` when `prefers-reduced-motion`

- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 2 (Structure): Integration
  - [ ] Component integrated into `DiamondShape`
  - [ ] `useReducedMotion()` hook for conditional rendering
  - [ ] Static version shown when reduced motion preferred

- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 3 (Surface): Visual polish
  - [ ] JetBrains Mono font applied
  - [ ] Color: `--text-secondary` (#E0E0E0)
  - [ ] Background: `--bg-surface-1` (#1A1A1A)

- [ ] Pass 3 — Layer 4 (Interaction): Accessibility verification
  - [ ] Screen reader test (NVDA/VoiceOver): hears complete code once
  - [ ] Reduced motion test: static display when enabled
  - [ ] Animation completes in 3s

**Delegation:**
```
/implement "Create ScreenSafeTyping.tsx component with CSS steps() typing animation. CRITICAL: Use aria-hidden on visual animation + sr-only parallel content for screen readers. Implement useReducedMotion() check for static fallback. Add CSS keyframes to globals.css. Test with screen reader if possible."
```

**Verification:**
```bash
npm run build
npx playwright test --grep "typing"
# Manual: Enable VoiceOver, verify complete code announced once
```

